<tr id="S2.T1.4.1.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="S2.T1.4.1.8.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.8.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.8.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;"><span id="S2.T1.4.1.8.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Number</span></span></span>
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.8.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.8.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;"><span id="S2.T1.4.1.8.1.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Processing</span></span></span>
</span></span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">Integer Calculation</td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">CWE-128, CWE-191, CWE-193, CWE-369, CWE-1335</td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.4.1.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">Data Size Calculation</td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">CWE-467, CWE-469</td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.4.1.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="S2.T1.4.1.10.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.10.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.10.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.10.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;"><span id="S2.T1.4.1.10.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sensitive Info</span></span></span>
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.10.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="S2.T1.4.1.10.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;"><span id="S2.T1.4.1.10.1.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Exposure</span></span></span>
</span></span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">Process Exposure</td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">CWE-214</td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.4.1.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">Log Exposure</td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">CWE-532</td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.4.1.12" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="S2.T1.4.1.12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DoS Attack</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">Untrusted Data</td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">CWE-502</td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.4.1.13" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">Improper Control</td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">CWE-119</td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.4.1.14" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="S2.T1.4.1.14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Injection</span></td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.14.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">Command Injection</td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.14.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">CWE-78</td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T1.4.1.15" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.15.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">SQL Injection</td>
<td id="S2.T1.4.1.15.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1.25pt;padding-bottom:1.25pt;">CWE-89</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Code review is a common practice in modern software development processes. It is usually formalized as a generation task <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\rightarrow cmt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\rightarrow cmt</annotation></semantics></math>, which takes the program <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> as input and outputs natural language comments <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cmt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cmt</annotation></semantics></math> to indicate potential issues.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we define secure code review as a multiple-goal task <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\rightarrow(cat,\ loc,\ cmt)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\rightarrow(cat,\ loc,\ cmt)</annotation></semantics></math>, which takes a program <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> as input and outputs the category <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cat" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cat</annotation></semantics></math> of the security issues and its location <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="loc" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">loc</annotation></semantics></math>, along with a natural language review comment <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="cmt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">cmt</annotation></semantics></math> for further explanation. This task is generally more challenging than regular code review, as it also requires the accurate identification of security issues and locations. With identified security issues and locations, we can evaluate the effectiveness of an approach more objectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">II-B</span> </span><span id="S2.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Motivating Example to Reduce False Positives</span></h3>

